Exp:-10 Creation and Execution of Child process using fork().

Aim:- To write and execute a C program that creates a child process, waits for its termination and displays its PID.

Requirements:- Ubuntu OS, Virtual Box and GCC compiler.

Steps:-
1) Open the Ubuntu Terminal.
2) Create a C program using: `nano exp10.c`
3) Program used:
#include <stdio.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <unistd.h>
int main() {
  int pid;
  printf("Parent PID: %d\n", getpid());
  pid = fork();
  if (pid < 0) {
    printf("Fork failed \n");
  }
  else if (pid == 0)
  {
    printf("Child PID: %d\n", getpid());
    printf("child process is running\n");
  }
  else {
    wait(NULL);
    printf("child process terminated\n");
  }
  return 0;
}
4) Save the file using Ctrl+O, press Enter and exit using Ctrl+X.
5) Compile the program: `gcc exp10.c -o exp10`
6) Execute the program: `./exp10`
7) Observe the parent PID, child PID and termination message.

Result:-
Successfully created a child process using fork(), retrieved its PID using getpid() and waited for its termination using wait(NULL).
